ready-to-send templates: a concise WhatsApp/chat message for quick coordination and a complete onboarding email with post-setup steps.
Quick Chat / WhatsApp Checklist

Hi [Client Name],
Before we connect your WhatsApp Business number to chain-bot, please make sure you have these 5 things ready:
1. Facebook Admin Login: A Facebook account with Admin access to your company's Meta Business Portfolio (if you don’t have one yet, you can create it during setup).
2. Primary Phone in Hand: You’ll need physical access to the phone running your WhatsApp Business number to receive an in-app verification code.
3. Updated WhatsApp Business App: Ensure your app is updated to the latest version (v2.24.17 or newer). Note: Regular personal WhatsApp accounts will not work.
4. Two-Step Verification Turned Off: Temporarily disable your 6-digit PIN in the app (Settings > Account > Two-step verification). You can turn it back on after setup.
5. Valid Payment Card: A credit or debit card ready to add to your Meta Business billing settings (required by Meta for sending outbound API/template messages).
Important notes during & after setup:
• When prompted inside your WhatsApp app, tap Confirm to share your chat history so your past messages sync to our platform.
• Someone on your team must open the WhatsApp Business app on the primary phone at least once every 14 days to keep the API connection active.
Reply once you're ready, and I’ll share the connection link!


Client Onboarding Email Template

Subject: Action Required: Preparing to Connect Your WhatsApp Business Number
Hi [Client Name],
To connect your existing WhatsApp Business App number to chain-bot without losing access to your mobile app, we will walk you through Meta’s official self-serve connection flow. You will not need to share any passwords or API keys with us.
Please complete this quick checklist before clicking our setup link:

1. Pre-Setup Checklist

• Meta Business Portfolio Admin Access: Log in using a Facebook profile that has full Admin permissions for your company's Meta Business Portfolio. (If you do not have one yet, you can create a new portfolio during the setup popup using your legal business name, address, and HTTPS website URL).
• Primary Phone on Hand: Keep the smartphone holding your active WhatsApp Business SIM card nearby. Meta will send a verification code directly inside your WhatsApp app that you will need to copy and paste.
• Updated WhatsApp Business App: Confirm you are using the WhatsApp Business App (version 2.24.17 or higher). Standard personal WhatsApp accounts are not supported.
• Disable Two-Step Verification Temporarily: Open your WhatsApp Business App and go to Settings > Account > Two-step verification to turn off your 6-digit PIN. You can re-enable it once setup is complete.
• Confirm Number Eligibility: Ensure your number is not currently connected to another WhatsApp API provider and does not carry a Meta Verified / Official Business Account blue checkmark.

2. Two Quick Steps During / After Setup

1. Approve Chat History Sync: During the setup process, you will receive a prompt inside your WhatsApp Business App asking to share your chat history. Please tap Confirm so your recent contacts and messages sync to chain-bot (this cannot be turned on later).
2. Add a Payment Method in Meta: While replies inside your mobile app remain free, Meta requires a valid credit or debit card on file in your Meta Business Billing settings before chain-bot can send automated or template messages.

3. Good to Know After Connecting

• 14-Day App Activity Rule: To keep the integration active, someone must open the WhatsApp Business App on your primary phone at least once every 14 days.
• Feature Adjustments: Group chats and voice/video calls will stay on your phone and will not sync to the platform. Disappearing messages and "View Once" media are automatically disabled on 1:1 chats while connected.
Let me know once you have completed the checklist above, and we can get started!
Best regards,
[Kenny / Chain Innovations Team]